ok - a dirty copy and an unpushed copy with a verified recorded bundle are both kept
ok - a copy whose tip is on no remote but whose content already landed is removed by the teardown landed rule
ok - a project clone under a Firstmate home is enumerated, budgeted as a container, and swept
ok - a failing git worktree remove leaves the copy, is reported, exits 1, and is attempted once
ok - apply never forces, cleans, unlocks, recursively deletes or calls treehouse
ok - a load above the limit skips only the sizing, says so in the report and the record, and listing, classes and apply still run
ok - 6 skipped runs in a row raise one wake, none while the streak stands, and again after a sized run breaks it
ok - du runs one at a time as nice -n 20 du -sk, with and without a deadline
ok - sizes are cached by copy path and mtime and expire with cache-max-age
ok - a copy nested in another copy is subtracted from the enclosing one
ok - the budget wake names budget, total and the five largest copies with class, fires once, and fires again after a drop and a new overrun
ok - a pool budget and a container budget that go over together raise one wake
ok - apply raises the budget wake once through the wake queue
ok - a scan cut at its time bound wakes only on bytes it measured and records no completed scan
ok - a registered copy whose directory is gone counts as 0 KiB, so it never latches a budget record
ok - a git or lsof call that cannot finish inside check's time leaves the copy UNCLASSIFIED and the wake is still printed in time
ok - run from the root home, a lane's proven copy is reaped, its own live record holds a copy, and an unreadable lane holds every copy
ok - an outer copy that holds a dirty inner copy is held and apply keeps both, even when git status cannot see the inner copy
ok - an outer copy is held while an inner copy exists, reaped by the next run once it is removed, and not held by a registration whose directory is gone
ok - a zero-padded or non-numeric FM_CHECK_TIMEOUT no longer aborts the check
ok - a copy holding an ignored file that exists nowhere else is kept, regenerable machinery is reaped, and a failed listing holds the copy
ok - graft output alone is reaped, and a custom .ignore or a clone below graft/ still holds the copy
ok - a check whose enumeration is slow stops looking for clones at its time bound and still prints the wake for the clones it reached
ok - a check stops looking at a home's project clones at its time bound
ok - a cut check keeps the standing budgets it did not reach and counts toward the streak of skipped runs
